<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49439" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turbātor</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				troubler</i>, <i>disquieter</i>, <i>disturber</i> (not ante-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turbatores vulgi erant tribuni plebis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					4, 48, 1</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulgi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 4,
					2, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plebis (Gracchi et Saturnini),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					3, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Germaniae (Arminius),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 55</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 30</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">otii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 3, 17</span></i>
			
			<i>fin.—Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turbatores belli,</span>”
				<i>stirrers up of war</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					2, 16, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
